METRICS = [
('rewards/equation_reward_func/mean','Fraction of sampled completions passing the arithmetic verifier.','Track held-out improvement; training improvement alone can be memorization.'),
('rewards/format_reward_func/mean','Fraction passing the tag regex after restoring the prompt’s opening <think>.','If this rises alone, the policy is learning formatting rather than arithmetic.'),
('reward','Mean format + equation score, range [0,2].','Separate the two components; total reward can hide a stagnant solve rate.'),
('rewards/.../std; reward_std','Dispersion of each component/total across logged sampled completions. In this pinned version reward_std is batch-wide.','Do not confuse it with per-prompt standard deviation or uncertainty in held-out accuracy.'),
('frac_reward_zero_std','Fraction of prompt groups whose total rewards all match.','Near 1 means no relative task signal; inspect whether all candidates fail or all succeed. Eval G=1 makes this 1 by construction.'),
('loss','Minimized clipped policy surrogate plus weighted KL, with masks/normalization.','Its scale/sign depends on centering and lengths. A low or near-zero loss is not evidence of arithmetic skill.'),
('grad_norm','Global norm of trainable gradients before max_grad_norm clipping.','Finite nonzero norms show a signal; repeated spikes suggest unstable updates. Zero may be equal group rewards.'),
('learning_rate','Scheduler’s reported step LR.','Check that continuation follows the original horizon; a 1-step horizon would decay immediately.'),
('kl','Sample-based, token-masked reference/current KL estimator (with the pinned correction).','Look for controlled drift alongside solve-rate gains. Exploding KL with flat accuracy is concerning; beta=0 can remove the key.'),
('entropy','Mean full-vocabulary entropy at generated token positions, in nats.','Falling entropy can mean confidence or collapse; inspect reward diversity and held-out outputs together.'),
('clip_ratio/region_mean','Fraction of active token ratios clipped in the direction that would improve the surrogate.','It is not simply the fraction outside [0.8,1.2]. Near zero early is expected with fresh rollouts/one iteration; high values indicate stale/aggressive updates.'),
('clip_ratio/low_mean; high_mean; low_min; high_max','Sign-aware low/high clipping rates and extrema across sequences.','Locate whether positive- or negative-advantage samples dominate clipping.'),
('completions/mean_length; min_length; max_length','Generated token counts, including ending tokens as counted by TRL.','Growing length can reflect useful reasoning or wasted budget. Inspect the actual text.'),
('completions/clipped_ratio','Fraction of completions hitting the generation cap without normal termination.','High values can cause missing closing tags/answers. Check length limits before interpreting zero rewards.'),
('step_time','Sum of timed training_step calls in an accumulation window. Includes rollout work done there, excludes evaluation/optimizer overhead outside the calls.','Compare to lab wall_step_seconds; neither should be read as whole-run throughput.'),
('eval_* / eval_runtime / eval_loss','Held-out versions of applicable metrics, generation wall time and the evaluation surrogate.','Use solve rate, format, truncation, n, and samples. With G_eval=1 the centered task advantage is zero, so eval_loss is not a useful task measure.'),
('train_runtime; train_loss; train_*_per_second','Whole train() call timing, mean reported training loss and Trainer throughput counters.','Resumed calls report their own timings; sample counters are not distinct-prompt or generated-token throughput.'),
('GPU device used / free','Device-wide CUDA memory snapshot including other processes and vLLM.','Do not equate this with live training tensors; other processes can explain differences.'),
('torch allocated / reserved / peak allocated / peak reserved','Live tensor bytes, allocator-owned blocks, and high-water marks since reset at step begin.','Reserved ≥ allocated is normal. Peaks diagnose OOM headroom; PyTorch counters can miss non-PyTorch allocations.'),
('lab: joint / Wilson interval / n','Both rewards pass; 95% binomial Wilson solve-rate interval; number of held-out prompts.','Small classroom holdouts are noisy. Intervals are descriptive; reused validation rows and related tasks limit inference.'),
]
